<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Miani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1843">1843</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Miani was fought on 17 February 1843 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyderabad-sindh">Hyderabad</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a>, where a small British-Indian army under General Sir Charles Napier defeated the much larger forces of the Talpur <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amir">amirs</a> of Sindh. Napier won again at Dubba in March, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> annexed Sindh, which was attached to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mumbai">Bombay</a> Presidency.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-miani.jpg" alt="Battle of Miani" width="320" height="207" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Edward Armitage · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Edward_Armitage_(1817-96)_-_The_Battle_of_Meeanee,_17_February_1843_-_RCIN_407185_-_Royal_Collection.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
